  "published": "2026-09-29T15:56:51.147Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.1.0 — Darnelix.Webp, a WebP codec written entirely in C#: one managed assembly, no native code, zero runtime dependencies. Decode: lossy and lossless still images, with alpha, into RGBA32, BGRA32, ARGB32, RGB24 or BGR24; cropped and scaled decode; incremental decode from bytes as they arrive; header-only feature reads; animated WebP frame by frame onto a composited canvas. Encode: lossy or lossless still images, with alpha, a target size or PSNR, sharp YUV and near-lossless preprocessing; animated WebP from full-canvas frames with per-frame durations, a loop count and a background colour. The same input and options produce the same bytes, with or without the optional worker threads. A truncated, corrupt or unsupported file raises a WebpException subtype. Container metadata and animation parameters are edited with the companion tool, Darnelix.Webp.Cli.",
  "title": "Darnelix.Webp — pure-C# WebP codec",
  "verbatimVersion": "1.1.0",
